  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1100 PM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nWednesday through Sunday:\n\nEnsembles generally suggest the quieter weather pattern will\ncontinue with high pressure building back into the region later\nin the week. Aloft, things become a bit more active with some\nshortwave activity swinging down late in the week but the issue\nis that there remains too much dry air to cause much of any \nprecip chances. The pattern will switch up into the weekend \nlarge scale ridging building overhead behind a trough sweeping \nthrough Friday. Models suggest a mild chance for precip with the\ntrough but a lot of uncertainty remains with how that should \npan out. Overall the general pattern is suggestive of largely \ndry conditions until at least early next week.\n\nKuroski",
